│Current repo: parity-bot/issu█▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀█                             │
└─────────────────────────────█ New comment                                                                                      █─────────────────────────────┘
┌─ [1] Repositories ──────────█  Write   Preview  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── █─────────────────────────────┐
│ ★  Owner       Name         █  Agreed, and I think the README should say so explicitly. Here's what I'd add under Keys:        █                             │
│ ☆  parity-bot  issue-fixture█                                                                                              ▁▁  █━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━│
│ ☆  parity-bot  dotfiles     █  - `j` / `k` move one line and stop at either end of the file; they never wrap around.           █                             │
│ ☆  parity-bot  hello-world  █  - `G` jumps to the last line and `g` to the first.                                              █                             │
│ ☆  parity-bot  lazy-demo    █  - `J` / `K` move by hunk, and stop at the first and the last hunk.                              █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  I also checked the three cases you listed against the current build. All three behave as        █                             │
│                             █  described, so I don't think we need a code change here, just the docs. If you want, I can       █                             │
│                             █  open a follow-up for the wrap-around idea, since a few people asked for it in the               █                             │
│                             █  discussion, but I'd keep it behind a setting so the default stays the same as today.            █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
└─────────────────────────────█  One more thing: the help panel lists `j` as "Line down" but the footer says "Down". We          █                             │
┌─ [2] Pull Requests ─────────█  should pick one. I'd go with the help panel's wording because it's more specific, and the       █he defaults when it is empty,│
│ #  Status  Author      Title█  footer has room for it at 100 columns.                                                          █lse changes for people who   │
│ 8  open    parity-bot  A pul█                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  Steps I ran:                                                                                    █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  1. Open a file longer than the screen                                                           █                             │
│                             █  2. Press `G`                                                                                    █                             │
│                             █  3. Press `j`, then `k`, then `g`                                                                █                             │
│                             █  4. Press `J` and `K` on a file with three hunks                                                 █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  Every one of them stopped where the docs will say it stops. The only surprise was `K` on        █                             │
│                             █  the first hunk, which does nothing rather than wrapping to the last one, and that matches       █                             │
│                             █  the rest.                                                                                       █                             │
└─────────────────────────────█                                                                                                  █                             │
┌─ [3] Issues ────────────────█  Finally, the screenshot in the README is from 0.5 and still shows the old title bar. I'll       █                             │
│ #   Status  Author         T█  refresh it in the same PR, and add one of the diff view with a cursor on a hunk header,         █                             │
│ 12  open    parity-friend  C█  since that's the part people ask about.                                                         █                             │
│ 11  closed  parity-bot     C█                                                                                                  █                             │
│ 10  open    parity-bot     C█  A few notes for whoever picks up the wrap-around follow-up:                                     █                             │
│ 9   open    parity-friend  C█                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  - keep the default as it is today                                                               █                             │
│                             █  - put the setting next to the other viewer settings                                             █                             │
│                             █  - make `G` and `g` respect it too, so the keys stay consistent                                  █                             │
│                             █  - add a snapshot for the wrapped position at both widths                                        █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  I'll link this thread from the follow-up so the context isn't lost. If anything in the          █                             │
│                             █  list above looks wrong, say so here and I'll fix it before the PR goes up.                      █                             │
└─────────────────────────────█                                                                                                  █                             │
┌─ [4] Workflows (empty) ─────█  Thanks again for the careful report. The steps made this quick to check.                        █                             │
